        "collapsible_row_imrEM6": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What are MoonAnchors?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonAnchors are the mounting hardware that attach MoonShade to your vehicle. Every MoonShade setup requires them. The type you need depends on your vehicle's surface and how permanent you want the mount to be.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_UcLXCg": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need MoonAnchors to use MoonShade?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes — every MoonShade requires anchors to mount. MoonShade RV is the one exception: it slides directly into a keder rail with no separate anchor needed.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_T9nrei": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are MoonAnchors permanent?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Most are fully removable with no surface damage. Suction and magnetic anchors come on and off in seconds. MoonMounts create a stronger semi-permanent bond — designed for vans and larger rigs that stay set up for longer periods. No drilling needed.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_FcfR6H": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I use the same MoonAnchors on different vehicles?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>It depends on the anchor type. Suction and magnetic anchors can move between compatible surfaces. MoonMounts are typically matched to a specific surface type. Check each anchor listing for compatibility details.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_wLNNcC": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do MoonAnchors hold up in wind?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Customers have reported MoonShade (OG) holding in gusts up to 30–40 mph with MoonAnchors. For high-wind conditions, pairing anchors with guy lines is the recommended setup.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_f4U6dK": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What's the difference between MoonAnchors and MoonMounts?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p> MoonAnchors is the product family name covering all anchor types. MoonMounts are a specific anchor within that family — a semi-permanent mount designed for vans and larger rigs that need a stronger hold than suction or magnetic options provide.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
